tests.proves:
Setup: a granted window on air, a kept pass on a layer, and an approved WEB OPEN http://10.0.0.5:9924/w/<token> line run.

The token is in none of:
- STATE, CONTEXT or EYE;
- the journal or the log;
- a built support bundle;
- the module's recorded lines;
- InputLabels after labelling that input;
- the twin wire with SendSecrets off.

The settings file holds it only under Secret.

A raw window URL written into a loaded show draws black, publishes unkept:// and lights the Super Check row.

risks:
WebView2 is unproven off a real machine. Three things must hold:
- the certificate exception covers the window's wss socket;
- the document-created observer runs under the window's CSP;
- WebMessageReceived reaches the host.

CI can't construct WebView2 (OPEN L26), so these are §22 walk rows, unwalked until filled. A same-machine show avoids TLS.
